<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African mohair prices lower at sixth summer sale.</title>
<headline>S.African mohair prices lower at sixth summer sale.</headline>
<dateline>PORT ELIZABETH, South Africa 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African mohair prices for the sixth summer sale were lower, the Mohair Board said on Wednesday. There was still very good demand for sale.</p>
<p>Of the 1,382 bales offered 59 percent was sold.</p>
<p>Approximate prices in South African cents a kg:</p>
<p>Adults	  long	 2,100-3,650	(2,300-2,660)</p>
<p>		  medium     1,800-2,000	(1,850-2,360)</p>
<p>		  short	1,750-1,890	(1,850-2,320)</p>
<p>Young Goats   long	 2,300-2,800	(2,450-4,050)</p>
<p>		  medium     2,050-2,050	(2,300-2,800)</p>
<p>		  short	     -	     (2,400-3,500)</p>
<p>Fine Kids     long	 7,600-12,850     (5,200-13,252)</p>
<p>		  medium     4,252-6,000	(3,500-6,850)</p>
<p>		  short	3,800-4,600	(3,270-4,600)</p>
<p>The last sale of the season is scheduled for June 18, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27-11 482 1003</p>
</text>
